{"hits": {"hits": [{"links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/468989?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/468989?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/468989?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/468989?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/468989?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/468989?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A468989"}, "created": "1998-04-07T00:00:00+00:00", "updated": "2023-03-07T04:14:14.765531+00:00", "metadata": {"authors": [{"full_name": "Guo, Xiao-feng"}], "publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "58", "artid": "114033", "year": 1998, "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.D"}], "texkeys": ["Guo:1998rd"], "abstracts": [{"value": "In deeply inelastic lepton-nucleus scattering (DIS), the average jet transverse momentum is broadened because of the multiple scattering in the nuclear medium. The size of jet broadening is proportional to the multi-parton correlation functions inside nuclei. We show that at leading order, jet broadening in DIS and nulcear enhancement in di-jet momentum imbalance and Drell-Yan $< q_T^2 > $ share the same four-parton correlation functions. We argue that jet broadening in DIS provide an indenpendent measurement of the four-parton correlation functions and a test of QCD treatment of multiple scattering."}], "control_number": 468989, "dois": [{"value": "10.1103/PhysRevD.58.114033"}], "arxiv_eprints": [{"value": "hep-ph/9804234"}], "titles": [{"title": "Jet broadening in deeply inelastic scattering"}, {"title": "Jet broadening in deeply inelastic scattering."}, {"title": "Jet broadening in deeply inelastic scattering"}], "author_count": 1, "document_type": ["article"]}, "id": "468989"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=eprint%20hep-ph%2F9804234&size=3&page=1&fields=c